calib_detect.py — RealSense world calibration + SAM3 detector
                  + sequence-driven pick & place runner.

Per-frame px_per_mm is estimated from ArUco markers and written into
the GRIPPERS dict, so the gripper feasibility check works in real units.

Pick decision also looks at NEIGHBOURING detections:
  - parallel gripper: both finger footprints must be free of other parts
  - suction gripper : a disc around the cup centre must be free of other parts

Sequence behaviour (NEW):
  - Each sequence item may specify "count" (default 1): how many parts to
    pick from that tray. After every successful pick a NEW picture is
    taken (parts have shifted/are now gone).
  - If a detection cycle finds nothing acceptable, the runner asks the
    operator to *shake the plate*, waits for confirmation, and retries
    up to "retries" times before giving up on that item.

Keys:
  L           = click test point
  R           = clear clicked points
  SPACE       = lock/unlock calibration
  C           = clear marker history
  S           = save calibration
  D           = load calibration
  X           = run SAM3 detection on current frame (using ACTIVE_PART)
  1..9        = switch active part (by index in PARTS)
  P           = run pick & place SEQUENCE from sequence_robotic_arm.json
  ESC         = quit
"""

